window.docContents[167].resolve({"/5___-Representations-of-finite-groups___-Further-results/5___13___-Proof-of-the-classification-theorem-for-representations-of-___S_n___/c_lambda-is-proportional-to-an-idempotent/#Chapter5___Lemma5___13___3":{"contents":"Lemma 5.13.3. c_\\lambda is proportional to an idempotent. Namely, c_\\lambda^2 = \\frac{n!}{|P_\\lambda||Q_\\lambda| \\dim V_\\lambda} c_\\lambda.\n\nProof. Lemma 5.13.1 implies that c_\\lambda^2 is proportional to c_\\lambda. Also, it is easy to see that the trace of c_\\lambda in the regular representation is n! |P_\\lambda|^{-1} |Q_\\lambda|^{-1} (as the coefficient of the identity element in c_\\lambda is |P_\\lambda|^{-1} |Q_\\lambda|^{-1}). This implies the statement. \\square\n\n\n\n","context":"Introduction to Representation Theory\t5. Representations of finite groups: Further results\t5.13. Proof of the classification theorem for representations of $S_n$\tc_lambda is proportional to an idempotent","header":"c_lambda is proportional to an idempotent","id":"/5___-Representations-of-finite-groups___-Further-results/5___13___-Proof-of-the-classification-theorem-for-representations-of-___S_n___/c_lambda-is-proportional-to-an-idempotent/#Chapter5___Lemma5___13___3"}});
